<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1773">1773</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lord Combermere</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stapleton <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">Cotton</a>, 1st Viscount Combermere, was a British cavalry commander. He led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>'s cavalry in the Peninsular War, including at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamanca">Salamanca</a> in 1812. As Commander-in-Chief in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1825 to 1830 he besieged and took the fortress of Bharatpur in January 1826, which had defied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-lake-1st-viscount-lake">Lord Lake</a> in 1805, and was made a viscount. He became a field marshal in 1855.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stapleton-cotton-1st-viscount-combermere.jpg" alt="Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mary Martha Pearson (née Dutton) (died 1871) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stapleton_Cotton,_1st_Viscount_Combermere_by_Mary_Martha_Pearson_(n%C3%A9e_Dutton).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
